      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/nov/02/unions-google-workers-uk-employment-rights</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Prospect to hold workplace sessions and recruit members under agreement with tech company&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Trade unions are expected to make further inroads into big tech companies in the UK after new rights for unions to access workplaces &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/30/tuc-leader-union-recognition-private-sectoraccess"&gt;came into force&lt;/a&gt;, with Google UK signing an agreement on Monday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Prospect union has reached an agreement with Google to begin organising among about 7,000 workers across its UK operations, including YouTube but&amp;nbsp;excluding DeepMind.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/nov/02/unions-google-workers-uk-employment-rights"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
