      <title>US tech stocks recover after selloff spooks investors over AI spending</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/03/us-tech-stocks-recovery-ai-spending</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Midterms didn’t appear to have huge impact, though predicted wins for Democrats could mean more regulation&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;US tech stocks made a recovery on Tuesday afternoon after a selloff spooked investors over &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/technology/artificialintelligenceai"&gt;AI&lt;/a&gt; spending.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Tuesday’s &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-midterm-elections-2026"&gt;midterm elections&lt;/a&gt; didn’t appear to have a huge impact on Wall Street, though investors are predicting Democrats get at least a majority in the House and potentially gain seats in the Senate, which could lead to more AI regulation.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/03/us-tech-stocks-recovery-ai-spending"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
